WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.119
In September, when Anne started school, Marilla was worried.

2
00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:11.144
Anne was a strange girl. How would she make friends?

3
00:00:11.145 --> 00:00:13.871
How would she stay quiet in the classroom?

4
00:00:13.872 --> 00:00:18.617
But after her first day, Anne came home excited and happy.

5
00:00:18.618 --> 00:00:25.155
"I like school!" Anne declared. "I don't like the teacher, Mr. Phillips, though.

6
00:00:25.156 --> 00:00:30.137
He said my spelling was terrible and held it up for everybody to see!"

7
00:00:30.138 --> 00:00:33.156
"Anne, don't say that about your teacher.

8
00:00:33.157 --> 00:00:36.399
I hope you were a good girl," said Marilla.

9
00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:44.574
"I was," answered Anne. "I sit with Diana near the window, and we can see the Lake of Shining Waters.

10
00:00:44.575 --> 00:00:47.346
I am in a lower class than Diana though.

11
00:00:47.347 --> 00:00:51.154
She is on the fifth book, and I am on the fourth book.

12
00:00:51.155 --> 00:00:56.982
There are many nice girls in school, and we had fun playing at lunchtime.

13
00:00:56.983 --> 00:01:04.113
"And Jane Andrews told Ruby Gillis she heard Minnie McPherson say that I had a pretty nose.

14
00:01:04.114 --> 00:01:09.077
That is the first compliment I have ever had in my life, Marilla!

15
00:01:09.078 --> 00:01:13.394
Do I have a pretty nose? I know you'll tell me the truth."

16
00:01:13.395 --> 00:01:16.483
"Your nose is all right," Marilla said.

17
00:01:16.484 --> 00:01:23.305
Secretly she thought that Anne's nose was remarkably pretty, but Marilla had no intention of telling her so.

18
00:01:23.306 --> 00:01:28.161
Three weeks passed, and Anne and Diana were walking to school one morning.

19
00:01:28.162 --> 00:01:33.957
"Gilbert Blythe will be in school today," said Diana. "He's been away at his cousins'.

20
00:01:33.958 --> 00:01:38.912
He's so handsome, Anne, and he teases the girls terribly."

21
00:01:38.913 --> 00:01:44.607
From Diana's voice it was clear that Diana liked being teased by Gilbert Blythe.

22
00:01:44.608 --> 00:01:47.926
"Gilbert's in your class," Diana went on.

23
00:01:47.927 --> 00:01:52.126
"He's on the fourth book because he missed school when his father was sick.

24
00:01:52.127 --> 00:01:54.665
He's usually at the top of the class though.

25
00:01:54.666 --> 00:01:57.296
You're at the top of the class now, Anne."

26
00:01:57.297 --> 00:02:00.798
"I'm glad Gilbert is coming back," said Anne.

27
00:02:00.799 --> 00:02:07.609
"I don't feel proud about being at the top of a class with little boys and girls who are only nine years old!"

28
00:02:07.610 --> 00:02:16.336
The girls went into the classroom. "That's Gilbert Blythe sitting across from you, Anne," said Diana. "Isn't he handsome?"

29
00:02:16.337 --> 00:02:24.664
Anne looked. She had lots of time to look because Gilbert was busy tying Ruby Gillis' long golden braid to her chair.

30
00:02:24.665 --> 00:02:29.733
Gilbert was a tall boy with curly brown hair and a cheeky smile.

31
00:02:29.734 --> 00:02:36.431
When Ruby Gillis tried to stand up, she fell back screaming, thinking that her hair was being pulled out!

32
00:02:36.432 --> 00:02:40.218
Everybody stared at her, and she started to cry.

33
00:02:40.219 --> 00:02:43.678
Gilbert read his book and looked very serious.

34
00:02:43.679 --> 00:02:48.403
But when everyone was quiet again, he looked at Anne and winked at her.

35
00:02:48.404 --> 00:02:53.338
"I think your Gilbert Blythe is handsome," whispered Anne to Diana.

36
00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:59.296
"But he's very bold. It isn't polite to wink at a girl he doesn't know."

37
00:02:59.297 --> 00:03:03.397
In the afternoon Gilbert tried to get Anne's attention again.

38
00:03:03.398 --> 00:03:09.070
Mr. Phillips, the teacher, was in the back of the room, explaining math to an older girl.

39
00:03:09.071 --> 00:03:16.104
The other students were drawing pictures on their slates, eating apples, whispering, or playing with some crickets.

40
00:03:16.105 --> 00:03:20.304
Gilbert Blythe tried to make Anne look at him, without success.

41
00:03:20.305 --> 00:03:25.958
Anne stared out the window at the Lake of Shining Waters, lost in her own world.

42
00:03:25.959 --> 00:03:32.838
Usually girls did look at Gilbert. He thought, "That redheaded Shirley girl should look at me."

43
00:03:32.839 --> 00:03:37.598
He reached across the aisle and grabbed the end of Anne's long red braid.

44
00:03:37.599 --> 00:03:43.162
He held it out and said in a loud whisper, "Carrots! Carrots!" This

45
00:03:43.163 --> 00:03:47.807
time Anne did look at him—and she did more than look. She

46
00:03:47.808 --> 00:03:51.155
jumped up and stared fiercely at Gilbert. "You

47
00:03:51.156 --> 00:03:59.703
mean, hateful boy!" she shouted. "How dare you!" And then— thwack!

48
00:03:59.704 --> 00:04:02.678
Anne cracked her slate on Gilbert's head.

49
00:04:02.679 --> 00:04:09.319
The students at Avonlea School always enjoyed a scene, and this was an especially good one.

50
00:04:09.320 --> 00:04:13.428
Diana gasped. Ruby Gillis began to cry again.

51
00:04:13.429 --> 00:04:16.345
Mr. Phillips stalked to the front of the classroom.

52
00:04:16.346 --> 00:04:20.423
"Anne Shirley, what happened just now?" he said angrily.

53
00:04:20.424 --> 00:04:27.029
Anne did not answer. It was too embarrassing to tell everybody that Gilbert had called her "Carrots."

54
00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:32.410
Gilbert spoke. "It was my fault. I teased her," he admitted.

55
00:04:32.411 --> 00:04:40.173
Mr. Phillips ignored Gilbert. "Anne, stand in front of the board for the rest of the afternoon," he told her.

56
00:04:40.174 --> 00:04:43.665
With a pale, stony face, Anne obeyed.

57
00:04:43.666 --> 00:04:52.588
Mr. Phillips wrote on the board above her head, "Ann Shirley has a very bad temper. Ann Shirley must control her temper."

58
00:04:52.589 --> 00:05:00.413
Then the teacher read the words aloud so that everybody, even the youngest children who could not read, understood.

59
00:05:00.414 --> 00:05:06.048
Anne stood there all afternoon. She didn't cry because she was still angry.

60
00:05:06.049 --> 00:05:11.514
Anne thought, "I'll never speak to Gilbert Blythe again!"

61
00:05:11.515 --> 00:05:18.795
When school finally ended, Anne marched out and waited for Diana on the porch. Gilbert approached her.

62
00:05:18.796 --> 00:05:23.418
"Sorry I teased you, Anne," he whispered. "I'm really sorry."

63
00:05:23.419 --> 00:05:29.860
Anne ignored him. Gilbert put a candy that said "You are sweet" on the ledge near Anne.

64
00:05:29.861 --> 00:05:38.843
Anne picked it up carefully, dropped it on the floor, and ground it into a fine powder under her shoe. Then she started walking.

65
00:05:38.844 --> 00:05:44.722
"Oh, Anne," said Diana. "How could you ignore his apology?"

66
00:05:44.723 --> 00:05:50.317
"I will never forgive Gilbert Blythe," Anne retorted furiously.

67
00:05:50.318 --> 00:05:54.073
"And Mr. Phillips spelled my name without an 'e'!"

68
00:05:54.074 --> 00:05:57.836
"Gilbert teases all the girls, Anne," Diana said.

69
00:05:57.837 --> 00:06:02.009
"He laughs at my hair because it's so black, and calls me 'Crow.'

70
00:06:02.010 --> 00:06:06.188
He's never said sorry to any girl before today!"

71
00:06:06.189 --> 00:06:12.616
"There's a big difference between 'Crow' and 'Carrots,' Diana!" Anne said with a sniff.

72
00:06:12.617 --> 00:06:17.220
The next day at school, Mr. Phillips' mood had not improved.

73
00:06:17.221 --> 00:06:20.234
He spotted Anne talking to Charlie Sloane.

74
00:06:20.235 --> 00:06:26.744
"Anne Shirley, since you like boys so much, you will sit with Gilbert Blythe," said Mr. Phillips.

75
00:06:26.745 --> 00:06:30.936
The other boys laughed. Anne did not move.

76
00:06:30.937 --> 00:06:34.709
"Anne, obey me at once," the teacher said.

77
00:06:34.710 --> 00:06:37.745
For a moment it seemed Anne would never move.

78
00:06:37.746 --> 00:06:44.980
But at last she got up, sat down beside Gilbert, and buried her face in her arms on the desk.

79
00:06:44.981 --> 00:06:51.471
To sit next to a boy was bad enough, but to sit next to Gilbert Blythe was unbearable.

80
00:06:51.472 --> 00:07:01.183
When school ended, Anne picked up everything from her desk—all her books, her pen and ink, and piled them onto her cracked slate.

81
00:07:01.184 --> 00:07:05.397
"Why are you taking everything home, Anne?" Diana asked.

82
00:07:05.398 --> 00:07:09.323
"I'm not coming to school anymore," said Anne.

83
00:07:09.324 --> 00:07:15.098
When Anne got home, she told Marilla she had finished school—forever.

84
00:07:15.099 --> 00:07:18.165
"Nonsense," said Marilla.

85
00:07:18.166 --> 00:07:21.599
"Marilla, I've been insulted."

86
00:07:21.600 --> 00:07:25.243
"You'll go tomorrow," was Marilla's answer.

87
00:07:25.244 --> 00:07:31.640
"Oh no," said Anne. "I'm not going back. I'll study at home."

88
00:07:31.641 --> 00:07:37.768
Marilla knew Anne was stubborn, and so she let Anne study at home—for the time being.

89
00:07:37.769 --> 00:07:42.019
She hoped that Anne would miss her schoolmates and return to school soon.

90
00:07:42.020 --> 00:07:52.437
"But it is Anne," Marilla acknowledged with a sigh. "So anything could happen."

